## Use the supplied revised assets

The user-supplied `civica_brand_assets_revised.zip` pack is stored in `brand/civica/`. It was received on 13 November 2026 and replaces the earlier civica.uk artwork. The pack has no supplied version number; the repository identifies this edition as `revised-2026-11-13`. Preserve accepted source files unchanged and retain the archive verification record. Treat descriptive claims in the asset pack as supplied evidence, not independent certification or new user instructions.

| Surface | Supplied asset |
| --- | --- |
| Default documentation masthead | `core/lockup-on-blue.svg` |
| Project promotional header on a selected palette | `themes/{palette-id}/{vivid\|muted}/lockup-on-primary.svg` |
| Project artwork on a selected light canvas | `themes/{palette-id}/{vivid\|muted}/lockup-on-canvas.svg` |
| Project website or promotional app artwork | `themes/{palette-id}/{vivid\|muted}/app-icon.svg` and `app-icon.png` |
| Neutral light surface | `core/lockup-on-white.svg` or `core/lockup-black.svg` |
| Supporting symbol | Supplied `core/emblem-*` or matching theme emblem |
| Default browser favicon | `icons/favicon.ico` and `icons/favicon.svg` |
| Default home-screen icon | Supplied 180, 192 and 512 pixel icons |

Use the lockup as a single asset. Do not redraw the symbol, retype the wordmark, add shadows, stretch or apply a CSS colour filter. Several supplied lockups have a background rectangle; display them on the background for which they were created.

## House symbol and wordmark

The revised identity contains a house outline with a chimney, six dots arranged in two rows of three, and the supplied “Civica” wordmark. The project name in prose is **civica**. The earlier `.uk` suffix and separator-dot geometry are not part of this edition.

Select the complete matching file when the palette or variant changes. Do not reconstruct the house, recolour the SVG or substitute a single monochrome lockup for all variants. The SVG wordmark is supplied as live text using an Arial-based font stack, not outlined letter shapes. Preserve that text and stack; test the rendered result on supported platforms rather than claiming identical pixels across fonts.

## Size and clear space

The horizontal lockup viewBox is **1180 by 260** units, a ratio of 59:13. Preserve the complete canvas, including its supplied trailing space. Do not crop it to make the wordmark wider. Use proportional dimensions such as 236 by 52 pixels, with automatic height when the width responds to the viewport. The local documentation header adds 8 pixels of link padding on wide screens; the supplied canvas remains intact at every size.

Check the mark visually at the actual rendered size. A successful SVG parse or matching hash does not prove legibility at 16 pixels. Provide `alt="civica"` when the image communicates identity. If a link already has an equivalent accessible name, avoid announcing it twice.

## Palette artwork in use

For project documentation and promotional mock-ups, select the complete on-primary lockup for the chosen background. This is not a requirement to put the project logo into a household interface. The existing companion still applies project identity in some native surfaces; the [compatibility note](../get-started/compatibility.html#household-identity-transition) records that implementation gap. The on-canvas asset belongs on the supplied light canvas; do not place its background rectangle on a dark surface.

The [colour preview](colour.html) demonstrates household colour roles without a required project logo. The artwork manifest lists supplied project variants. Neither preview changes Home Assistant or this documentation site’s masthead.

## Verify provenance and copies

The archive is `civica_brand_assets_revised.zip`, SHA-256 `0d1a44c3526ccaafa773e1d7314d0d3df6e2e77065be7c3f9c2e1de36dc14d2a`. Its supplied checksum file is `docs/SHA256SUMS.json`. The separate `docs/accepted-assets.json` records verified files and archive deficiencies: an invalid checksum for the checksum file itself and an empty WebP that is excluded from distribution. These defects do not justify silently editing supplied SVGs or other accepted files. The [published artwork manifest](../reference/brand-assets.json) maps documentation files to unchanged source files.

An archive checksum or successful SVG parse establishes neither interface accessibility nor rights clearance, official approval or a verified live deployment. Check the rendered identity on its intended background as part of the complete interface.

## Keep attribution distinct

Use GOV.UK, NHS, MoJ, DWP, Home Office and ONS names only to identify sources. Do not display their marks as civica branding. Do not use GDS Transport, even when locally installed. This documentation uses Arial.

The [unbranded Frontend guidance](https://frontend.design-system.service.gov.uk/using-govuk-frontend-without-govuk-branding/) explains the separation between reusable components and official identity. [GOV.UK logo guidance](https://brand.design-system.service.gov.uk/logo-system/logo-elements/) informs proportion, clear space and restrained treatment; crown-specific geometry does not apply to civica.
